      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I’m glad you came in. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Well, nice to meet you... what brings me in is, uh, I just always feel like I’ve got this motor humming under my skin whenever I’m supposed to sit still. Like, if I'm in a staff meeting at the school where I work. Actually, they just bought these brand new floor buffers for the hallways, and let me tell you, you have to use a specific kind of wax or it leaves these terrible streaks, and the principal is real particular about the shine. He actually got on my case about it last Tuesday, which is ridiculous because I told him the supplier sent the wrong bucket... \n\nBut anyway, yeah, in those meetings, or even during church event briefings—I help set up the fellowship hall on weekends—I just can't stay put. I end up shifting around in my chair the whole time, standing up in the back of the room, or just finding some excuse to go check the trash cans or something so I can move around. It just drives me crazy to just sit there.",
