      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Act without thinking? Uh, no, I don't really think I do that. I actually try to plan things out. \n\nLike with the supply closet at the school, you really have to think ahead, especially with the heavy-duty trash bags. If you don't get the 55-gallon ones ordered by the first of the month, the cafeteria ladies just stuff the smaller ones until they split wide open. And let me tell you, cleaning up sloppy joes from the floor tile grout is an absolute nightmare. I actually had to use an old toothbrush on it a couple weeks ago because the sealant on the grout completely wore off near the serving line. My wife actually asked why I was packing a toothbrush in my lunchbox, and I had to explain to her that the district won't approve the budget for the industrial grout brushes... \n\nBut, uh, wait. What were we talking about? Oh, doing things without thinking. Yeah, no, I haven't really noticed that. I'm usually pretty careful.",
