      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Trouble focusing? No, I don't think so. When I need to get something done, I get it done. \n\nLike, uh, just yesterday I spent a solid two hours fixing the pneumatic closer on the main entrance door. You know those heavy commercial doors with the metal arms at the top? If you don't adjust the tension valve exactly right with an Allen wrench, the wind catches it and it slams so hard it rattles the glass in the front office. And the secretary, Brenda, she absolutely hates that. She’s got this whole collection of little ceramic frogs lined up on her desk—don't ask me why, I think her grandkids paint them or something—and a few months ago the door slammed and knocked one right off. Shattered everywhere. I had to get the special fine-dust attachment for the shop vac just to get all the little painted pieces out of the carpet fibers, because regular vacuums just spit that stuff right back out... \n\nBut, uh, anyway. What was it you asked? Trouble paying attention? No, I don't have that problem. I can focus on whatever I'm working on just fine.",
