    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often feel restless or fidgety even when you’re trying not to move?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Fidgety? Well, like I was saying about those staff meetings, I guess my legs just always want to bounce. Even when I'm just at home in my recliner trying to watch the evening news. \n\nIt's one of those faux-leather ones, you know? Actually, the metal track on the footrest is starting to squeak really bad every time I shift my weight. I keep meaning to bring home some of the WD-40 Specialist spray from work—not the regular blue and yellow can, you gotta use the dry silicone one. People don't realize that regular WD-40 actually attracts dirt and ruins the tracks over time. They just spray it on door hinges and a month later it's a black, gummy mess. We had this guy, the new night shift guy, Gary, who went around spraying every single locker hinge in the boys' locker room with the regular stuff because he thought he was being helpful. It took me three days with an industrial citrus degreaser to fix it. And let me tell you, the smell of that orange degreaser, it just gets right up into your sinuses and lingers for a week. You can even taste it when you eat your sandwich at lunch... \n\nBut, uh, sorry. What were we talking about? Oh, feeling restless. I don't know, I just don't really like sitting still, I guess.",
