    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often interrupt people or finish their sentences?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S016",
      "patient_response": "Interrupting people? Yeah, I guess I do that sometimes. It's just... well, like when my supervisor or one of the church staff starts telling me what they need done, I usually know exactly where they're going with it, so I just jump in and finish their sentence for them. Though, I guess sometimes I get it wrong and they have to correct me. \n\nLike last week, Pastor Dave was trying to tell me about setting up the folding chairs in the fellowship hall, and I just jumped in and said, \"Yeah, yeah, 50 chairs in a semicircle, got it.\" But he was actually trying to tell me they needed the long banquet tables set up for a potluck. Have you ever tried to move those heavy wooden banquet tables by yourself? They're the old ones, solid core, probably weigh a hundred pounds each. You gotta lock the metal legs in just right or the whole thing collapses. We had one collapse during the Easter breakfast three years ago—scrambled eggs and little smokies everywhere. And let me tell you, getting dried egg off of industrial carpet is almost impossible. You have to use this special enzyme cleaner, and even then, if you don't extract it right away with the carpet machine, it leaves this weird yellowish stain that catches the light... \n\nBut, uh, wait, what did you ask me? Interrupting? Yeah, I do jump in before people finish talking sometimes. I just want to get to work, you know?",
